 "studies": {
  "outside-readiness-stock-v2": {
   "study": "outside-readiness-stock-v2",
   "kind": "outside_readiness_stock_study",
   "title": "Corrected outside-query controls on a frozen unseen stock cohort",
   "evidence_only": true,
   "certificates": "none",
   "scope": "One corrected control-readiness opening on a frozen, previously unqueried stock cohort. Both control openings ran as frozen and returned the required literal labels; the byte-backed readiness gate then refused admission, so no holdout request was issued and all six planned mode/class cells stay Unknown. It is not a model, a qualification, an admission repair, a new calibration score, a retry of the old study or a game run.",
   "method": "The frozen pre-control plan bound source, build, catalog, inputs, selection, requests, predictions, controls, protocol, structural expectations and stop policy before the first control request. This ledger re-checks the archived bytes, re-derives the canonical 82-file study-tree digest, derives the versioned 30-file contract closure from the two constant declarations it parses as data, and checks that every closure file is present in the freeze with the same hash. It then re-derives the control arithmetic and the retained raw hashes. It does not run the collector, driver, auditor, bundle builder, evaluator, reporter, scorer, model or game.",
   "survives": "The two corrected controls are complete, released and returned the required literal labels: six positive requests succeeded and six invalid-vehicle requests failed. The independent pre-request build index equals the request's effective argument on all twelve rows, the opening graph equals the post graph on both openings, and all ten owned PID/start identities are gone after the driver exited, verified by a post-exit audit rather than a self-attestation. Controls are known controls, not holdout predictions and not independent capability votes.",
   "stopped": "The frozen freeze.json binds an 82-file study-tree source manifest. The accepted readiness contract requires frozen.source_files to be exactly the versioned 30-file closure and requires the runtime phase's source_sha256 to equal that closure's digest. The collector recorded the 82-file digest instead. Those two values cannot both be true of one measured opening. Correcting the recorded binding would rewrite a measured field after the controls; changing the closure would change the frozen source digest and require new controls. The no-retry rule forbids both, so the unchanged checker is left refusing and both digests stay recorded.",
   "result": "unknown",
   "limits": "The outcome is Unknown and limited: zero of six planned holdout requests were issued, so no holdout accuracy, precision or recall exists; those denominators stay null and not estimable, never 0%. The two controls are control-readiness observations, not a decision law, not holdout votes and not a qualification. No geographic negative, service, spawning, sustained-navigation, stable-water or admission claim follows. The old PL-1294 six Unknowns are unchanged and the new controls do not rescue them. Replaying the retained checks needs the exact licensed game bytes and CRPs named by hash in bundle.json; they stay in the same-owner private blade holding and are neither in this repository nor attached to the issue. A fresh clone cannot reproduce the full verify: it expects the untracked .build/Cs1Harness.dll and the original absolute staged-source path. File identity is not memory attestation, compiler trust or strict-no-mods evidence. Assemble_v2, finalize_v2 and report_v2 were written after the controls, are outside the frozen measurement closure, and measure and qualify nothing. No certificate, app adoption, model refit, public merge or Shelf page follows.",
